# yosys technology-anchored metrics flow (frozen harness file).
# Maps the design to the bundled academic Nangate45 standard-cell library
# (typical corner, from The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD-flow-scripts) and
# reports REAL units: mapped standard-cell area in um^2 and an abc `stime`
# critical-path estimate in ps.
#
# Snapshot two-pass abc: `design -save` snapshots the pre-map netlist; the
# FIRST abc maps it and `stat -liberty` reports logic area on that mapped
# netlist (pre-buffer, comparable across designs). `design -load` restores
# the snapshot and the SECOND abc maps again, then applies fanout buffering
# and sizing (buffer;upsize;dnsize) before `stime`: without buffering, the
# wireload delay of unbuffered high-fanout nets (reset/config broadcast,
# wide buses) dominates the report by 2-3 orders of magnitude on
# realistic-scale designs (measured: 5084 ns unbuffered vs 6 ns buffered on
# a ~1M-gate design with ~20 levels of real logic depth). The second pass
# cannot share the first pass's mapped state (yosys skips abc when there is
# nothing left to map), hence the snapshot + remap; abc is deterministic so
# the area and timing figures come from the same mapping. Buffers inserted
# for timing are real but small (<10% of logic) and are not counted in the
# reported area.
# Memories stay as $mem_v2 (SRAM/ROM macros, credited separately as bits);
# macro read paths terminate at the blackbox boundary and are not part of
# the measured critical path. The delay/area here cover the mapped logic +
# flops. This flow feeds the resource/timing gates and the primary tokens/s
# metric. Invoked by evaluate.py with {FILES}/{LIB} substituted into a temp
# copy.
read_verilog -sv {FILES}
hierarchy -check -top msh_chip_top
proc
flatten
opt_expr
opt_clean
memory -nomap
opt -fast
techmap
opt -fast
dfflibmap -liberty {LIB}
design -save preabc
abc -liberty {LIB} -script +strash;dretime;map;topo
opt_clean
stat -liberty {LIB}
design -load preabc
abc -liberty {LIB} -script +strash;dretime;map;topo;buffer;upsize;dnsize;topo;stime,-c
